# Appendix B. All 26 Feature Computations

The 26 engineered features used by the family-stratified GPR, with exact RDKit API calls and NaN handling rules. All NaN values after computation are imputed to the family median from the training set; if the family median is also NaN (no training compounds have a finite value), the global training median is used as the fallback.

| **#** | **Feature** | **RDKit API** | **NaN Handling** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | MW | Descriptors.MolWt(mol) | Family median |
| 2 | LogP | Descriptors.MolLogP(mol) | Family median |
| 3 | TPSA | Descriptors.TPSA(mol) | 0.0 if no polar atoms |
| 4 | HBD | Lipinski.NumHDonors(mol) | 0 |
| 5 | HBA | Lipinski.NumHAcceptors(mol) | 0 |
| 6 | RotatableBonds | Lipinski.NumRotatableBonds(mol) | 0 |
| 7 | AromaticRings | Lipinski.NumAromaticRings(mol) | 0 |
| 8 | BertzCT | GraphDescriptors.BertzCT(mol) | Family median |
| 9 | Chi0v | GraphDescriptors.Chi0v(mol) | Family median |
| 10 | Chi1v | GraphDescriptors.Chi1v(mol) | Family median |
| 11 | Chi0n | GraphDescriptors.Chi0n(mol) | Family median |
| 12 | Chi1n | GraphDescriptors.Chi1n(mol) | Family median |
| 13 | LabuteASA | MolSurf.LabuteASA(mol) | Family median |
| 14 | GasteigerN_min | min over tertiary N Gasteiger charges | 0.0 if no tert N |
| 15 | GasteigerN_max | max over tertiary N Gasteiger charges | 0.0 if no tert N |
| 16 | GasteigerN_sum | sum over tertiary N Gasteiger charges | 0.0 |
| 17 | linker_length | SMARTS walk, see 3.3 | Family median |
| 18 | chain_min | Regex r"C\((\d+)\)" filter 2<n<=22 | Family median |
| 19 | chain_max | Same regex, max | Family median |
| 20 | chain_diff | chain_max - chain_min | 0 |
| 21 | chain_sum | chain_max + chain_min | Family median |
| 22 | is_HPRZ | SMARTS match -> 0/1 | 0 |
| 23 | is_MPRZ | SMARTS match -> 0/1 | 0 |
| 24 | is_H2EPRZ | SMARTS match -> 0/1 | 0 |
| 25 | is_DMBA | SMARTS match -> 0/1 | 0 |
| 26 | is_ester | ester count > amide count -> 1 | 0 |

Gasteiger partial charges (features 14-16) are computed by AllChem.ComputeGasteigerCharges(mol), after which the atom property _GasteigerCharge is read from every atom with atomic number 7 and degree 3 (tertiary nitrogen). GasteigerN_min is the minimum (most negative) such charge, GasteigerN_max is the maximum, and GasteigerN_sum is the sum across all tertiary nitrogens in the molecule. Features 17-21 are integer valued: linker_length comes from the SMARTS walk procedure in Section 3.3, and chain_min / chain_max come from the architecture string regex or SMILES fallback in Section 2.4.

