| Analog-anchored delta (v4, this spec) | 0.126 | 47% | 0.053 | 0.082 | 0.136 | 0.196 | 0.324 |

Per-family adaptive numbers from v4 (this specification): PE-Tris + GA-Tris combined MAE = 0.076 with 90% PI = ±0.13; sSS-Nonsym MAE = 0.136 with 90% PI = ±0.31; PE-Gallic MAE = 0.196 with 90% PI = ±0.45; Dialkoxybenzyl MAE = 0.324 with 90% PI = ±0.68. Measurement noise floor: triplicate SD mean = 0.051, max = 0.100.

# Appendix D. Delta Coefficient Table — Fully Populated

Every delta coefficient extractable from the v19 dataset. Reliability flags follow the n_pairs >= 5 AND SD <= 0.10 rule from Section 5.2. Entries flagged NULL with explanation indicate deltas that cannot currently be estimated.

| **delta_id** | **Family** | **Dim** | **From** | **To** | **Condition** | **delta** | **SE** | **n** | **Reliable** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| PEt-head-L2 | PEt | head_group | HPRZ | H2EPRZ | linker=2C | -0.045 | NaN | 1 | False | Single matched pair; use with Level 4 interaction |
| PEt-head-L3 | PEt | head_group | HPRZ | H2EPRZ | linker=3C | -0.055 | NaN | 1 | False | Single matched pair |
| PEt-head-L4 | PEt | head_group | HPRZ | H2EPRZ | linker=4C | -0.020 | NaN | 1 | False | Single matched pair |
| PEt-head-L5 | PEt | head_group | HPRZ | H2EPRZ | linker=5C | -0.140 | NaN | 1 | False | Single pair; large magnitude; drives interaction term |
| PEt-head-mean | PEt | head_group | HPRZ | H2EPRZ | mean over 4 linkers | -0.065 | 0.027 | 4 | False | Marginal n; linker-specific values preferred |
| PEt-linker-slope | PEt | linker_length | (any) | +1C | all heads pooled | +0.155 | 0.012 | 8 | True | Dominant reliable delta; slope 0.155 pKa/C |
| GAt-linker-slope | GAt | linker_length | (any) | +1C | HPRZ+MPRZ pooled | +0.134 | 0.013 | 6 | True | Reliable; slope 0.134 pKa/C |
| sSS-head-MPRZ | sSS | head_group | HPRZ | MPRZ | chain-pair matched | -0.014 | 0.017 | 82 | False | HIGH_UNCERTAINTY: SD=0.154 exceeds threshold |
| sSS-linkage-ester-amide | sSS | linkage_type | ester | amide | 4C HPRZ | NULL | NULL | 2 | False | NULL: n<3; requires 3+ matched ester/amide pairs to estimate |
| PEg-DMBA-linker-SS | PEg | linker_length | (any) | +1C | SS topology only | +0.082 | 0.055 | 3 | False | HIGH_UNCERTAINTY: SD=0.095 marginal; topology unlabeled |
| PEg-topology-SS-TT | PEg | topology | SS | TT | DMBA head | NULL | NULL | 0 | False | NULL: topology token not yet in arch_coarse; requires relabeling |
| DAB-all | DAB | (any) | (any) | (any) | (any) | NULL | NULL | 0 | False | NULL: n=12 heterogeneous; no matched pairs with n>=3 |
| GAt-head-HPRZ-MPRZ | GAt | head_group | HPRZ | MPRZ | 4C linker | NULL | NULL | 2 | False | NULL: n<3; requires additional matched pairs |
| GAt-head-HPRZ-H2EPRZ | GAt | head_group | HPRZ | H2EPRZ | any linker | NULL | NULL | 1 | False | NULL: n<3 |

The NULL rows identify experimental gaps that, once filled, would extend the delta table and enable Level 3 / Level 4 predictions for currently-unsupported cases. The PEg-topology row in particular is a labeling task rather than a new-synthesis task: topology tokens for the 22 PE-gallic DMBA compounds can be extracted from the source literature (DOI ja1c05813) and added to the training dataset, after which PE-Gallic LOO-CV MAE is expected to drop from 0.196 to approximately 0.12.